| Q1 | conditional | The L flags are preserved independently of the headline, but the function is not total. `INCONCLUSIVE_SMALL_N` (#13) cannot be reached, `not_assessable` has no decision cell, and there is no cell for P valid with PA path-failed. |
| Q2 | conditional | PA with a random adapter is a control for learning from native memory, not "retention". `PA_RETENTION` will likely be null, so `ADAPTER_REGIME_LOSS` is misnamed. P step0 should reproduce the P0 artifact within tolerance. |
| Q3 | conditional | The `.05` floor is about 1% of the P0 mean (5.24 on val). I expect `P_VALID` to pass almost trivially, so it works only as a path/sensitivity sanity screen. |
| Q4 | conditional | An eligible target needs `K_real` at or below roughly the 10th-longest of the 20 train lengths. That makes the common ≥15/20 cohort likely unreachable. This is data-only and can be checked before the freeze. |
| Q5 | conditional | The CI level and method are not pinned, and the top-3 share formula is undefined. The runner drops copy-ineligible docs from the full-CE set too, so the copy/full "common subset" is vacuous. `bootstrap_paired` still mislabels the key `seeds_positive` (it counts documents). |
| Q6 | conditional | The unregistered seed does not hide the registered val documents. The runner also prints the full payload. Debug should use other documents or sealed outcome fields. |
| Q7 | disagree as written | 12 units × 100 updates already equals the 1,200 cap, and debug adds 20 updates plus 4 units. v0.2.1 also silently moves the cap from "2 CPU-hours" to 2h wall-clock. |
